    "https://jobs.latrobe.edu.au/en/job/544876/indigenous-employment-program-expression-of-interest": {
      "title": "Indigenous Employment Program- Expression of Interest",
      "description": "Indigenous Employment Program- Expression of Interest Job No.: 544876 Work type: Continuing, Fixed Term La Trobe University is strongly committed to providing employment opportunities to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples in all academic and professional roles and levels. Indigenous Australian candidates can register an Expression of Interest for consideration and notification of roles that may become available in the future. These details will remain on file for a period of twelve (12) months and actively matched against any suitable position that may arise during that time. Indigenous employment enquiries may be forwarded to the La Trobe Recruitment Team via email at Recruitment@latrobe.edu.au Advertised: 23/1/2011 Closing Date: Back to search results Apply now"
    },
    "https://jobs.latrobe.edu.au/en/job/571078/senior-coordinator-security-operations-and-incident-response": {
      "title": "Senior Coordinator, Security Operations, and Incident Response",
      "description": "Senior Coordinator, Security Operations, and Incident Response Job No.: 571078 Work type: Continuing HEO8 Full-time Continuing position La Trobe University’s Melbourne (Bundoora) campus location Hybrid working arrangements About the position La Trobe University is seeking an experienced security professional to coordinate operational security and security-related incident response across its campuses and sites. Reporting to the Senior Manager, Campus Safety, this University-wide role will coordinate day-to-day security services, incident and emergency response, event-security readiness, procedures, training, exercises, reporting and operational assurance. To be successful, you will have demonstrated experience in security operations, incident response, emergency response and operational readiness within a complex, multi-site environment. You will also have strong stakeholder-management, analytical and communication skills, with the ability to remain calm and accountable during incidents and disruption. Based at Bundoora, the role has University-wide responsibilities and requires regular travel to other campuses and sites. Essential Criteria Skills and knowledge required for the position A degree, extensive management expertise and supporting experience, or postgraduate qualifications and extensive relevant experience, or an equivalent alternate combination of relevant knowledge, training, and/or experience. Demonstrated security and safety knowledge and proven operational oversight and experience in a complex, multi-site working environment. Demonstrated experience coordinating security operations, incident response, emergency response and operational readiness in an active or 24/7 environment. Demonstrated experience managing or monitoring outsourced security services, service-level requirements, contractor performance and key performance indicators. Demonstrated ability to develop, implement and review operational procedures, response plans, training, exercises, and assurance activities. Demonstrated ability to analyse incident information, investigations, trends, and patterns and use operational data to provide initiative-taking recommendations and management briefings. Demonstrated ability to operate or effectively use incident-reporting and security-operations systems, with experience in platforms such as Gallagher Command Centre, Milestone Integrated CCTV desirable or the equivalent. Please see the position description for all other duties and skills and knowledge required for the position. Essential Compliance Requirements To hold this La Trobe University position, the occupant must: Hold, or be willing to undertake and pass, a Victorian Working with Children Check. Take personal accountability to comply with all University policies, procedures and legislative or regulatory obligations; including but not limited to TEQSA and the Higher Education Threshold Standards. Current Victorian driver licence with ‘Car’ listed under licence type. Hold a current Security Licence Benefits: • 17% employer contributed superannuation • On site childcare facilities • Flexible work arrangements, job-share applicants will be individually considered • Discounts for staff and their family members to study a range of La Trobe courses Why La Trobe: Help transform the lives of students, partners and communities now and in the future Develop your career at an innovative, global university where you’ll collaborate with community and industry to create impact. Enjoy working on our inspiring and stunning campuses – the perfect hub for industry, students and academics How to apply Closing date: By Sunday the 8 th of November 2026 Position Enquiries: Rita Rossi, Senior Manager, Campus Safety r.rossi@latrobe.edu.au Recruitment Enquiries: Madeleine Parker, First Nations Talent Acquisition Consultant m.parker@latrobe.edu.au Position description below: PD-HEO8 Senior Coordinator, Security Operations & Incident Response.pdf Please submit an online application ONLY and include the following documents: An up-to-date resume; Cover letter addressing your suitability for the position and; Separate document responding to each dot point of the key selection criteria Please scroll down to apply. All La Trobe University employees are bound by the Working with Children Act 2005. If you are successful, you will be required to hold a valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check prior to commencement. Based Violence (GBV Code). This aligns with our mission to create safe and respectful communities. Candidates will be asked during the recruitment process to declare whether they have ever been investigated for, or found to have engaged in, gender-based violence in previous employment and/or in legal proceedings and provide relevant information to assist in determining suitability. Gender-based violence means any form of physical or non-physical violence, harassment, abuse or threats based on gender, that results in, or is likely to result in harm, coercion, control, fear or deprivation liberty or autonomy. Advertised: 15/10/2026 Closing Date: 08/11/2026 Back to search results Apply now"
    },
    "https://jobs.latrobe.edu.au/en/job/571155/senior-lecturer-law": {
      "title": "Senior lecturer, Law",
      "description": "Senior lecturer, Law Job No.: 571155 Work type: Continuing Continuing position Full-time Based at either La Trobe University’s Bundoora or Bendigo campus. Level C Salary starting at $144,266 per annum + 17% superannuation Teaching focused About the position Lead the coordination and curriculum development of the Bachelor of Laws (Honours) and associated double degrees in a teaching-focused academic role (Level C). Responsibilities include course and subject coordination, curriculum design, student support and scholarly work to enhance teaching and learning. Experience teaching Priestley subjects is welcomed, particularly Equity and Trusts, Evidence, Criminal Procedure, and Legal Practice and Professional Conduct. Skills and Experience To be considered for this position, you will have PhD or equivalent in a relevant discipline and a primary degree in law (Bachelor of Laws or Juris Doctor). Demonstrated capacity to provide leadership at course/program level. Demonstrated effectiveness in teaching, curriculum development and subject coordination in face-to-face, blended and/or online modes with a commitment to excellence in teaching, as evidenced by sustained high results on student feedback on teaching surveys, teaching excellence awards or through other forms of evidence. Demonstrated evidence of innovative initiatives undertaken in the last three years that have improved the student experience, and the evaluation of effectiveness of these initiatives. Please refer to the Position Description for other duties, skills and experience required for this position. Welcome to Bundoora campus – Please click on the video link below: https://f.io/KDo0ceng Benefits: 17% employer contributed superannuation On site child care facilities Flexible work arrangements Discounts for staff and their family members to study a range of La Trobe courses How to apply Closing date: By 11:55 pm on Monday the 9 th of November 2026 Position Enquiries: Madelaine Chiam, Deputy Dean, Associate Dean Academic and Partnerships E: m.chiam@latrobe.edu.au ) Recruitment Enquiries: Madeleine Parker, Talent Acquisition Consultant E: m.parker@latrobe.edu.au Position description below: PD-Level-C-Teaching-Focused-Senior-Lecturer Only candidates with Full Working Rights in Australia may apply for this position. Please submit an online application ONLY and include the following documents: Cover letter addressing your suitability for the position; A separate document addressing each dot point of the Key Selection Criteria outlined under the “Essential Criteria; Skills and knowledge required for the position” section in the Position Description; and An up-to-date resume; Please scroll down to apply. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We welcome and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. La Trobe University is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workforce. We take an intersectional approach by actively supporting and encouraging people of all backgrounds and abilities to submit an application and aim to ensure that the recruitment and employee experience is as accessible and inclusive as possible. Flexibility in interview format will be offered to shortlisted candidates. All La Trobe University employees are bound by the Working with Children Act 2005. If you are successful, you will be required to hold a valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check prior to commencement . La Trobe University is committed to upholding the National Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence (GBV Code). This aligns with our mission to create safe and respectful communities. Candidates will be asked during the recruitment process to declare whether they have ever been investigated for, or found to have engaged in, gender-based violence in previous employment and/or in legal proceedings and provide relevant information to assist in determining suitability. Gender-based violence means any form of physical or non-physical violence, harassment, abuse or threats based on gender, that results in, or is likely to result in harm, coercion, control, fear or deprivation of liberty or autonomy. Advertised: 14/10/2026 Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Back to search results Apply now"
