    "https://jobs.latrobe.edu.au/en/job/569921/director-summer-disability-research-centre": {
      "title": "Director, Summer Disability Research Centre",
      "description": "Director, Summer Disability Research Centre Job No.: 569921 Work type: Fixed Term Fixed Term (4 years), Full-Time Professor Classification Level E Base salary from ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR LEVEL E + 17% superannuation About the position La Trobe University is seeking an outstanding research leader to take on the role of Director, The Summer Disability Research Centre, established through a strategic partnership between The Summer Foundation and the School of Psychology and Public Health at La Trobe University. This unique position is funded by The Summer Foundation and provides the opportunity to lead a nationally significant program of disability research. This is a rare opportunity to lead a purpose-driven research centre focused on generating evidence that improves housing, support and living outcomes for people with disability with high support needs. The Director will provide strategic leadership for the Centre's research agenda, secure competitive and philanthropic funding, build a high-performing, multidisciplinary research team, and ensure that research findings are translated into policy, practice, and systems change. Working at the intersection of research, policy, innovation and practice, the role draws on The Summer Foundation's extensive sector expertise, lived experience partnerships and national policy influence to generate rigorous evidence that informs policy reform, service innovation and systems change for people with disability with high support needs. The Director will foster a collaborative, inclusive research culture grounded in co-design and participatory research, ensuring people with lived experience of disability are central to the Centre’s work. Reporting to the Dean, School of Psychology and Public Health, the role contributes to the School’s research strategy, performance and external engagement at a national and international level. Skills and Experience To be considered for this position, you will have: A PhD or equivalent qualification in a relevant discipline such as psychology, public health, social sciences, rehabilitation or disability studies A distinguished record of research achievement at Associate Professor/Professor level or equivalent , including high-impact publications, competitive research funding and demonstrated research impact A strong track record of translating research into policy, practice or systems change, particularly within the disability, housing or health sectors Demonstrated experience providing strategic leadership to a research centre or large research program, including staff leadership and performance management Proven success in building and sustaining collaborative partnerships with government agencies, disability organisations, service providers and people with lived experience A deep understanding of issues affecting people with disability and a commitment to inclusive, accessible and ethical research practices Excellent communication, negotiation and stakeholder engagement skills Capacity to contribute to research supervision, HDR supervision and research capability development. A demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion, including creating respectful and accessible working environments Please refer to the Position Description for other duties, skills and experience required for this position. Benefits 17% employer contributed superannuation On site child care facilities Flexible work arrangements Discounts for staff and their family members to study a range of La Trobe courses How to apply Position Enquiries: Bircan Erbas Associate Dean Research & Industry Engagement, B.erbas@latrobe.edu.au Recruitment Enquiries: recruitment@latrobe.edu.au Only candidates with Full Working Rights in Australia may apply for this position. Please submit an online application ONLY and include the following documents: An up-to-date resume; and cover letter Response to Essential criteria Please scroll down to apply. Director Summer Foundation PD...docx We’d love to stay connected! If you would like to find out more about this School, please follow us on LinkedIn: School of Psychology and Public Health https://www.linkedin.com/company/school-of-psychology-and-public-health-la-trobe-university/ Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We welcome and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. Our commitment to diversity and inclusion La Trobe University is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workforce. We take an intersectional approach by actively supporting and encouraging people of all backgrounds and abilities to submit an application and aim to ensure that the recruitment and employee experience is as accessible and inclusive as possible. Flexibility in interview format will be offered to shortlisted candidates. Our commitment to safety All La Trobe University employees are bound by the Working with Children Act 2005. If you are successful, you will be required to hold a valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check prior to commencement. National Code on Gender Based Violence in Higher Education La Trobe University is committed to upholding the National Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence (GBV Code). This aligns with our mission to create safe and respectful communities. Candidates will be asked during the recruitment process to declare whether they have ever been investigated for, or found to have engaged in, gender-based violence in previous employment and/or in legal proceedings and provide relevant information to assist in determining suitability. Gender-based violence means any form of physical or non-physical violence, harassment, abuse or threats based on gender, that results in, or is likely to result in harm, coercion, control, fear or deprivation of liberty or autonomy. Why La Trobe Develop your career at an innovative, global university where you’ll collaborate with community and industry to create impact. Enjoy working on our inspiring and stunning campuses – the perfect hub for industry, students and academics. Help transform the lives of students, partners and communities now and in the future. Advertised: 19/10/2026 Closing Date: 14/11/2026 Back to search results Apply now"
    },
    "https://jobs.latrobe.edu.au/en/job/570953/learning-support-advisor": {
      "title": "Learning Support Advisor",
      "description": "Learning Support Advisor Job No.: 570953 Work type: Fixed Term HEO7 Full-time position Fixed term until 31/06/2027 The position is based at the Northern Study Hub in Broadmeadows and Epping – incumbents will need to be on site Take your career in exciting, rewarding directions About the position The Study Hub Learning Support Advisors identify and implement best practice in tertiary student engagement, learning, retention and course completion support. The support is provided within the community, in our purpose-built Northern Study Hub facilities at Broadmeadows and Epping. The Northern Study Hub is led by La Trobe University, with funding from the Australian Government. This means that the incumbent will be a La Trobe University employee but will work with students from any/all government-funded tertiary providers. The position is responsible for delivering tailored support- in academic skills, digital literacy, tertiary attainment and student wellbeing - as well as coordinating student engagement activities and fostering an inclusive and supportive study environment within the Study Hub. You will be working collaboratively with university and TAFE stakeholders, community partners, and students to enhance student participation and success in higher education. Skills and Experience To be considered for this position, you will have: • An undergraduate degree in any area, with at least 4 years subsequent experience in adult learning, student support or higher education environments; or an equivalent alternate combination of relevant knowledge, training and/or experience. • Experience in the delivery of high-quality student-centred learning, especially in relation to supporting university transition, student engagement, academic skill development, and course completions. • Intercultural understanding and/or multicultural lived experience, particularly in relation to the impacts and expectations these experiences can have on university studies. The ability to converse in language/s other than English, would be highly regarded. Please refer to the Position Description for other duties, skills and experience required for this position. Benefits: • 17% employer contributed superannuation • Flexible work arrangements • Discounts for staff and their family members to study a range of La Trobe courses How to apply Closing date: Sunday the 1st of November 2026 - Applicants are encouraged to apply early. Applications will be reviewed as they come in. Position Enquiries: Sam Sterling, Director, Northern Suburbs Study Hub via email, sam.sterling@latrobe.edu.au Recruitment Enquiries: Madeleine Parker, Talent Acquisition Consultant, via email m.parker@latrobe.edu.au Position description below: Study Hub Learning Support Advisor PD Only candidates with Full Working Rights in Australia may apply for this position. Please submit an online application ONLY and include the following documents: • Cover letter • An up-to-date resume; and • A separate document addressing each bullet point under the Essential Criteria ‘Skills and knowledge required for the position’, which is in the position description. Please scroll down to apply. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We welcome and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. La Trobe University is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workforce. We take an intersectional approach by actively supporting and encouraging people of all backgrounds and abilities to submit an application and aim to ensure that the recruitment and employee experience is as accessible and inclusive as possible. Flexibility in interview format will be offered to shortlisted candidates. All La Trobe University employees are bound by the Working with Children Act 2005. If you are successful, you will be required to hold a valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check prior to commencement. Based Violence (GBV Code). This aligns with our mission to create safe and respectful communities. Candidates will be asked during the recruitment process to declare whether they have ever been investigated for, or found to have engaged in, gender-based violence in previous employment and/or in legal proceedings and provide relevant information to assist in determining suitability. Gender-based violence means any form of physical or non-physical violence, harassment, abuse or threats based on gender, that results in, or is likely to result in harm, coercion, control, fear or deprivation liberty or autonomy. Advertised: 19/10/2026 Closing Date: 01/11/2026 Back to search results Apply now"
    },
    "https://jobs.latrobe.edu.au/en/job/571047/senior-coordinator-peak-scholars-program": {
      "title": "Senior Coordinator, PEAK Scholars Program",
      "description": "Senior Coordinator, PEAK Scholars Program Job No.: 571047 Work type: Fixed Term HEO7 Full-time Fixed-term position until 31/12/2031 Can be based at any of La Trobe University’s regional campuses Hybrid working arrangements About the position The PEAK Scholars Program forms part of La Trobe University’s Regional Pathway Program and is a new initiative scheduled for implementation in 2027. The Senior Coordinator will work closely with the Manager to shape and develop the program, including its design, delivery approach and evaluation framework. Working collaboratively with regional campuses and University-wide stakeholders, the Senior Coordinator will lead student engagement initiatives, develop strategic partnerships, and oversee program evaluation, reporting and continuous improvement. The position will also drive the development of scalable, student-centred approaches that build leadership capability, foster peer connections and improve transition outcomes for regional and equity cohort students. The role oversees an integrated program of scholarships, leadership development, mentoring, peer engagement, and industry and community connections, with a focus on strengthening belonging, engagement and success for regional students and is a wonderful opportunity to make a meaningful contribution to educational equity and regional engagement while positioning the PEAK Scholars Program as a flagship initiative that supports students to thrive at La Trobe University. The role requires regular travel to La Trobe’s regional campuses, with occasional out-of-hours work and overnight stays to support program delivery, student engagement and University events. Essential Criteria Skills and knowledge required for the position An undergraduate degree in any area relevant to the position with at least 4 years subsequent experience; or extensive experience and management expertise; or an equivalent alternate combination of relevant knowledge, training and/or experience. Excellent interpersonal skills, especially the capacity to work collaboratively and cooperatively in small teams. Demonstrated organisation and problem-solving skills, with an ability to manage several different projects concurrently. Demonstrated high level of self-motivation and personal management skills. Demonstrated ability to develop, foster and maintain productive relationships with internal and external stakeholders, including students, academic and professional staff, community organisations, industry partners and philanthropic stakeholders, to achieve strategic program outcomes. Demonstrated knowledge of student transition, engagement and leadership development principles, with the ability to design and deliver initiatives that enhance student belonging, participation and success for regional and equity cohort students. Please see the position description for all other Duties and Skills and knowledge required for the position Benefits: 17% employer contributed superannuation On site childcare facilities Flexible work arrangements, job-share applicants will be individually considered Discounts for staff and their family members to study a range of La Trobe courses Why La Trobe: Help transform the lives of students, partners and communities now and in the future Develop your career at an innovative, global university where you’ll collaborate with community and industry to create impact. Enjoy working on our inspiring and stunning campuses – the perfect hub for industry, students and academics How to apply Closing date: By Tuesday the 3 rd of November, 2026. Position Enquiries: Cherie Dyde, Manager, Regional Pathways & Access Programs C.Dyde@latrobe.edu.au Recruitment Enquiries: Madeleine Parker, First Nations Talent Acquisition Consultant m.parker@latrobe.edu.au Position description below: PEAK Senior Coordinator PD Please submit an online application ONLY and include the following documents: An up-to-date resume; and A cover letter addressing your suitability for the position relating to the key selection criteria Please scroll down to apply. All La Trobe University employees are bound by the Working with Children Act 2005. If you are successful, you will be required to hold a valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check prior to commencement. Based Violence (GBV Code). This aligns with our mission to create safe and respectful communities. Candidates will be asked during the recruitment process to declare whether they have ever been investigated for, or found to have engaged in, gender-based violence in previous employment and/or in legal proceedings and provide relevant information to assist in determining suitability. Gender-based violence means any form of physical or non-physical violence, harassment, abuse or threats based on gender, that results in, or is likely to result in harm, coercion, control, fear or deprivation liberty or autonomy. Advertised: 19/10/2026 Closing Date: 03/11/2026 Back to search results Apply now"
    },
    "https://jobs.latrobe.edu.au/en/job/570846/expression-of-interest-senior-officer-academic-services": {
      "title": "Expression of Interest - Senior Officer, Academic Services",
      "description": "Expression of Interest - Senior Officer, Academic Services Job No.: 570846 Work type: Fixed Term Full-Time, Fixed Term position until October 2027 Melbourne (Bundoora) Classification: HEO5 - Base salary from $84,084 + 17% superannuation Hybrid work model support About the position Reporting to the Senior Officer, Academic Services this position will contribute to the coordination of student lifecycle functions and workflows related to the broader Academic Services team. The incumbent will be responsible for working closely with peers and teams across the university to ensure a consistent approach to customer service delivery and consistent application of transactional activities and associated procedures. Skills and Experience To be considered for this position, you will have: Demonstrated depth or breadth of expertise developed through extensive relevant experience and application. Demonstrated ability to gain a conceptual understanding of relevant policies, procedures or systems and interpretation in the application of policy and/or precedent. Demonstrated capacity to organise work effectively and efficiently and deliver outputs in a timely manner. Demonstrated ability to work independently, follow established procedures with limited supervision and contribute positively to an effective team. High level proficiency in computer software packages including word processing, spreadsheets, databases, electronic mail, and the use of the internet as a research tool. Please refer to the Position Description for other duties, skills and experience required for this position. 50152851 Senior Officer, Academic Services PD.docx Benefits 17% superannuation Private Health Insurance discount Plus, many more, click HERE How to apply Closing Date: By 11:55pm on Thursday 5 th November 2026 Position Enquiries: Kelly Roberts, Senior Coordinator Academic Services Email: K.Roberts@latrobe.edu.au Recruitment Enquiries: Emma Fowler, Talent Acquisition Operations Officer, E.Fowler@latrobe.edu.au Please submit an online application ONLY and include the following documents: An up to date resume; and Cover Letter addressing key criteria for the role Only candidates with Full Working Rights in Australia may apply for this position. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We welcome and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. Our People At La Trobe, our people are the foundation of our success, with every role contributing to the delivery of our Strategic Plan 2025–2030 through meaningful work that makes a difference. How we work is as important as what we achieve, with our culture shaping the impact we create through everyday actions, collaboration, and shared accountability. Our sector-leading Leadership Academy develops leadership that is people first, purpose driven, intentional and embraces technology. By building the capability and confidence of all leaders, we create the conditions for individuals and teams to thrive, perform at their best and achieve shared success. Together, we foster an inclusive, respectful, and high-performing culture where excellence is recognised and celebrated. Our commitment to diversity and inclusion La Trobe University is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workforce. We take an intersectional approach by actively supporting and encouraging people of all backgrounds and abilities to submit an application and aim to ensure that the recruitment and employee experience is as accessible and inclusive as possible. Flexibility in interview format will be offered to shortlisted candidates. Our commitment to safety All La Trobe University employees are bound by the Working with Children Act 2005 . If you are successful, you will be required to hold a valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check prior to commencement. National Code on Gender Based Violence in Higher Education La Trobe University is committed to upholding the National Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence (GBV Code). This aligns with our mission to create safe and respectful communities. Candidates will be asked during the recruitment process to declare whether they have ever been investigated for, or found to have engaged in, gender-based violence in previous employment and/or in legal proceedings and provide relevant information to assist in determining suitability. Gender-based violence means any form of physical or non-physical violence, harassment, abuse or threats based on gender, that results in, or is likely to result in harm, coercion, control, fear or deprivation liberty or autonomy. Advertised: 28/10/2026 Closing Date: 05/11/2026 Back to search results Apply now"
    },
    "https://jobs.latrobe.edu.au/en/job/571115/senior-advisor-research-governance-assurance": {
      "title": "Senior Advisor, Research Governance & Assurance",
      "description": "Senior Advisor, Research Governance & Assurance Job No.: 571115 Work type: Continuing Full Time Continuing Position based at Bundoora Campus Salary range $106,472 - $117,127 plus 17% superannuation About the position The Ethics, Integrity and Biosafety (EIB) Team of the Research Office at La Trobe University provides holistic ethics, integrity and biosafety advice, support and service to researchers and to Committees. The Senior Advisor, Research Governance and Assurance will facilitate excellent research at La Trobe University by working with stakeholders across the university to develop, implement and manage governance structures to support the effective management of risk and compliance with industry standards and regulatory schemes. The position: Provides research governance advisory services, serving as the primary liaison for the University's research partners and internal stakeholders on matters relating to research ethics and compliance requirements. In conjunction with the Clinical Trials Platform, supports clinical trials governance by providing specialist advice and coordination to researchers undertaking clinical trials, ensuring compliance with applicable regulatory and governance frameworks. Provides research quality assurance by holding primary responsibility for the University's Risk-Based Monitoring (RBM) program and internal research audit activities. Develop and deliver RBM and internal research audit reports outlining the University's compliance status, key risk trends, and open/unresolved risks, ensuring timely reporting to relevant risk committees to support institutional oversight and decision-making. Skills and Experience To be considered for this position, you will have: A relevant tertiary qualification and experience in a relevant field such as research governance and ethics, compliance, tertiary education management, or health, medical or clinical research. Excellent written and verbal communication skills with an emphasis on the ability to evaluate, analyse and communicate information clearly to a range of audience. In-depth knowledge of relevant research governance frameworks and regulatory requirements, including the Australian Code for the Responsible Conduct of Research, the National Statement on Ethical Conduct in Human Research, ICH Good Clinical Practice, the National Clinical Trials Governance Framework, the Therapeutics Goods Act 1989 and the Gene Technology Act. Demonstrated experience providing high-level advisory services on research ethics and compliance requirements to researchers and/or external research partners, including the ability to interpret and translate complex regulatory requirements into practical guidance Please refer to the Position Description for other duties, skills and experience required for this position. PD - Senior Advisor Research Governance and Assurance.pdf Benefits 17% employer contributed superannuation Private Health Insurance discount Plus, many more, click HERE How to apply Closing date: By 11:55pm on Tuesday 17 th November 2026 Position Enquiries: Mark Li, Senior Manager, Ethics Integrity & Biosafety Email: Mark.Li@latrobe.edu.au Recruitment Enquiries: recruitment@latrobe.edu.au Only candidates with Full Working Rights in Australia may apply for this position. Please submit an online application ONLY and include the following documents: A cover letter outlining your relevant skills and experience required for the position and, An up-to-date resume. Please scroll down to apply. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We welcome and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. Our commitment to diversity and inclusion La Trobe University is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workforce. We take an intersectional approach by actively supporting and encouraging people of all backgrounds and abilities to submit an application and aim to ensure that the recruitment and employee experience is as accessible and inclusive as possible. Flexibility in interview format will be offered to shortlisted candidates. Our commitment to safety All La Trobe University employees are bound by the Working with Children Act 2005. If you are successful, you will be required to hold a valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check prior to commencement. National Code on Gender Based Violence in Higher Education La Trobe University is committed to upholding the National Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence (GBV Code). This aligns with our mission to create safe and respectful communities. Candidates will be asked during the recruitment process to declare whether they have ever been investigated for, or found to have engaged in, gender-based violence in previous employment and/or in legal proceedings and provide relevant information to assist in determining suitability. Gender-based violence means any form of physical or non-physical violence, harassment, abuse or threats based on gender, that results in, or is likely to result in harm, coercion, control, fear or deprivation liberty or autonomy. Advertised: 27/10/2026 Closing Date: 17/11/2026 Back to search results Apply now"
    }
